c(42, "§8.4; part 8 #4", "product-rule", "§8.4 experiment — if monetisation is introduced, charge for new capability, never for the free core: free_model_any stable at 44–47% in every era; a habit cap and subscriptions are what reviewers avoid in competitors; one will leave if charged; the only proposed model is a one-time purchase; the terms already reserve charging; do not cap habits, move widgets or statistics behind payment, or add ads — each contradicts a stated reason; if revenue is needed test an optional one-time purchase or tip for capabilities not yet shipped (watch, cloud backup, advanced frequency), announced in advance; measure the review stream for the first price complaints — 'the baseline is zero'.", "free core; charge only for unbuilt extras", "mixed", "free_model 45.35%; paywall_contrast 18.60%; one-time proposed 1; leave-if-charged 1", "product-rule", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["13903380759", "13546859530", "14227392787", "13682234945", "13936987753"], "", "")

c(43, "§8.5; §8.6; §8.7; part 8 #5; part 8 #6; part 8 #7", "insight", "§8.5 research — do the 1.0.15 goals cover the five frequency variants (N per week without fixed days; specific weekdays; every N days; monthly; custom interval)? where missing, the best-evidenced gap; where present, discoverability (one reviewer already credits 'a wide range of habit frequencies'). §8.6 Apple Watch — two E3 requests do not justify building one; check the developer's Discord/Reddit where requests are cheaper. §8.7 how independent are the ratings? — a prompt in every version, a launch cluster with the developer's surname, 28 one-line 5★, and website testimonials with generic names ('John Harris', 'Maria Smith') matching no reviewer — 'none of this indicates a problem with the product', but the rating is the main acquisition asset and its organic share is unknowable here; store rules on reviews from the developer's circle should be checked and the testimonials real or removed.", "n/a", "mixed", "REQ_FREQUENCY 5 variants; REQ_WATCH 2; ro/hu cluster 6; testimonials generic", "research", "limited evidence", "generalisable", ["13766824285", "13682367544", "14005146777", "14196935443", "12886063451"], "", "")

